"""
A moment in time as an RFC 3339 string with a time zone offset, for example
"2026-01-15T14:30:00Z" or "2026-01-15T09:30:00-05:00". Fractional seconds are
allowed. Input may also be "2026-01-15 14:30:00" with no offset, which is read
as UTC. Moments sent with different offsets compare as the same instant.
"""
scalar DateTime

"""
Free-form JSON, passed through as is. Services read it as a JSON object
(key/value pairs), so send an object rather than a list or a bare value.
"""
scalar JSON

"""
A UUID as text, for example "3f1c2b9e-8a4d-4e2f-9b1a-2c3d4e5f6a7b". A value
that is not a valid UUID is rejected before any query runs. The all-zero UUID
is returned as null.
"""
scalar UUID